WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:32.458
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna explained</b>

2
00:00:32.458 --> 00:00:37.125
<b>that a person who only displays external control</b>

3
00:00:37.125 --> 00:00:41.833
<b>but harbors desires within is a hypocrite.</b>

4
00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.625
<b>Here, Lord Krishna says</b>

5
00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:49.666
<b>that a person who follows Karma Yoga </b>
<b>is better than such a hypocrite.</b>

6
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.375
<b>Lord Krishna wishes to convey</b>

7
00:00:56.375 --> 00:01:04.416
<b>Hypocrites who pretend to control their senses </b>
<b>while secretly harboring intense cravings</b>

8
00:01:04.416 --> 00:01:08.666
<b>stands far beneath the person who honestly </b>
<b>acknowledges their desires</b>


9
00:01:08.666 --> 00:01:14.250
<b>and acts righteously according to the scripture.</b>

10
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:18.125
<b>The honest one is the person who </b>
<b>accepts their desires,</b>

11
00:01:18.125 --> 00:01:22.500
<b>does not falsely claim to </b>
<b>have control over their senses,</b>

12
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:29.250
<b>With this same honesty, one should aspire </b>
<b>to transform their condition.</b>

13
00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:33.375
<b>Through this path of selfless action </b>
<b>(Nishkam Karma Yoga),</b>

14
00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:37.041
<b>one can purify their mind and desires,</b>

15
00:01:37.041 --> 00:01:40.500
<b>ultimately achieving spiritual growth.</b>

16
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.916
<b>The emphasis here is on embracing truth.</b>

17
00:01:43.916 --> 00:01:45.291
<b>For instance,</b>

18
00:01:45.291 --> 00:01:47.541
<b>if someone wishes to become wealthy,</b>

19
00:01:47.541 --> 00:01:51.708
<b>the right approach is not to deny this truth.</b>

20
00:01:51.708 --> 00:01:53.333
<b>Instead, they should acknowledge this desire</b>

21
00:01:53.333 --> 00:02:00.833
<b>and then progress toward it through honest hard </b>
<b>work and righteous means of earning.</b>

22
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:05.875
<b>How great a lie it is when someone </b>
<b>internally harbors greed</b>

23
00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:11.416
<b>while outwardly pretending to </b>
<b>have no attraction to wealth.</b>

24
00:02:11.416 --> 00:02:13.958
<b>This is merely wearing a mask,</b>

25
00:02:13.958 --> 00:02:18.416
<b>and such people often end up committing </b>
<b>wrongdoings and crimes.</b>

26
00:02:18.416 --> 00:02:19.166
<b>However,</b>

27
00:02:19.166 --> 00:02:25.500
<b>one who doesn't lie makes sincere efforts to </b>
<b>fulfill their desires.</b>

28
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:32.125
<b>It's important to note that we're only speaking </b>
<b>of righteous desires here</b>

29
00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:39.666
<b>Desires that harm you or others </b>
<b>should always be avoided.</b>

30
00:02:39.666 --> 00:02:44.083
<b>The essence is simple: desires </b>
<b>are natural to human beings.</b>

31
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:46.875
<b>There's no need to deny them.</b>

32
00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:48.125
<b>What's needed is</b>

33
00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:53.291
<b>to acknowledge this truth and </b>
<b>perform one's duties according to divine wisdom.</b>

34
00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:56.291
<b>When you walk this path of truth,</b>

35
00:02:56.291 --> 00:03:04.500
<b>there will come a time when this very truth </b>
<b>will help control your cravings,</b>

36
00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:10.375
<b>leading you toward selfless action </b>
<b>and spiritual elevation."</b>

37
00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:21.125
<b>This verse emphasizes the importance of </b>
<b>always being truthful to oneself.</b>

38
00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:22.833
<b>In today's society,</b>

39
00:03:22.833 --> 00:03:26.000
<b>everyone is connected to one another.</b>

40
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.958
<b>We can talk to anyone at any time,</b>

41
00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:31.791
<b>and there are numerous platforms</b>

42
00:03:31.791 --> 00:03:37.875
<b>that constantly inform us about </b>
<b>what others are doing,</b>

43
00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:41.333
<b>eating, or where they are traveling.</b>

44
00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:42.500
<b>In such a scenario,</b>

45
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:47.083
<b>personal life is becoming a competition,</b>

46
00:03:47.083 --> 00:03:53.708
<b>where everyone wants to present their </b>
<b>best selves to the world.</b>

47
00:03:53.708 --> 00:04:00.875
<b>In the process of doing so, people often</b>
<b>forget their true selves.</b>

48
00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:10.208
<b>They try to present a version of themselves </b>
<b>to the world that has a false shine.</b>

49
00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:21.458
<b>This shine will not last, and ultimately, </b>
<b>they will face stress and sorrow.</b>

50
00:04:21.458 --> 00:04:24.375
<b>Consider, what is better?</b>

51
00:04:24.375 --> 00:04:26.666
<b>Being happy,</b>

52
00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.750
<b>or appearing to be happy?</b>

53
00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.375
<b>Becoming the best,</b>

54
00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:33.833
<b>or appearing to be the best?</b>

55
00:04:33.833 --> 00:04:39.125
<b>To make life truly beautiful, it is essential</b>

56
00:04:39.125 --> 00:04:43.333
<b>that we are honest with ourselves.</b>

57
00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:51.625
<b>We should look within and see our flaws,</b>
<b>our strengths,</b>

58
00:04:51.625 --> 00:04:56.708
<b>and whether we are genuinely </b>
<b>the person the world sees.</b>

59
00:04:56.708 --> 00:04:58.083
<b>If not,</b>

60
00:04:58.083 --> 00:05:02.250
<b>how can we become that person?</b>

61
00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:10.791
<b>We must work on our shortcomings</b>
<b>and polish our strengths.</b>

62
00:05:10.791 --> 00:05:17.583
<b>By walking on this path, you can become</b>
<b>a person whose shine is genuine,</b>

63
00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:25.750
<b>someone who shows the same face</b>
<b>to society as they do in their personal life.</b>

64
00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:31.333
<b>There is immense satisfaction </b>
<b>in living such a truthful life.</b>

65
00:05:31.333 --> 00:05:39.000
<b>Imagine it, and take a vow that you will</b>
<b>no longer lie to yourself.</b>

66
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.500
<b>You will only speak the truth and become better.</b>

67
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:53.041
<b>Whether it's a family on a small scale or</b>
<b>society on a larger scale,</b>

68
00:05:53.041 --> 00:06:00.291
<b>the beauty of both lies in the fact that </b>
<b>they are a mix of different people.</b>

69
00:06:00.291 --> 00:06:04.291
<b>Everyone has their own abilities and personality,</b>

70
00:06:04.291 --> 00:06:10.291
<b>like a garden with flowers of </b>
<b>different colors and fragrances.</b>

71
00:06:10.291 --> 00:06:12.708
<b>But</b>

72
00:06:12.708 --> 00:06:18.875
<b>would it be right to constantly compare </b>
<b>one flower in a garden to another?</b>

73
00:06:18.875 --> 00:06:27.500
<b>What would happen if one flower is given </b>
<b>more water and another is not?</b>

74
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.500
<b>Unfortunately,</b>

75
00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:34.416
<b>we often make this mistake</b>
<b>in our families and society.</b>

76
00:06:34.416 --> 00:06:37.500
<b>We constantly compare people.</b>

77
00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.125
<b>We give the water of praise to </b>
<b>one person, like a flower,</b>

78
00:06:41.125 --> 00:06:45.000
<b>while another remains without it.</b>

79
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.750
<b>Remember,</b>

80
00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:55.416
<b>you may have seen families where one </b>
<b>child is compared to another.</b>

81
00:06:55.416 --> 00:07:01.125
<b>One receives praise, and </b>
<b>the other receives criticism.</b>

82
00:07:01.125 --> 00:07:02.708
<b>How sad this is.</b>

83
00:07:02.708 --> 00:07:08.041
<b>This tendency forces people to wear a false mask.</b>

84
00:07:08.041 --> 00:07:10.916
<b>In the thirst for appreciation </b>
<b>and acceptance, people </b>

85
00:07:10.916 --> 00:07:15.666
<b>try to become something that</b>
<b>is different from their true nature.</b>

86
00:07:15.666 --> 00:07:19.500
<b>Those who are older and more experienced </b>
<b>in the family and society</b>

87
00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:25.500
<b>must take responsibility to stay away from </b>
<b>such negative comparisons.</b>

88
00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:31.916
<b>It is necessary for them to show everyone </b>
<b>the right path to move forward.</b>

89
00:07:31.916 --> 00:07:35.625
<b>For this, it is first essential to acknowledge</b>

90
00:07:35.625 --> 00:07:40.416
<b>that everyone has their </b>
<b>own personality and abilities.</b>

91
00:07:40.416 --> 00:07:46.291
<b>Then, help them identify these abilities </b>
<b>and accept their personality.</b>

92
00:07:46.291 --> 00:07:51.625
<b>Make them realize that they </b>
<b>are not inferior to anyone.</b>

93
00:07:51.625 --> 00:07:54.833
<b>Once their self-confidence is awakened,</b>

94
00:07:54.833 --> 00:08:02.125
<b>they only need a little guidance to overcome their weaknesses and enhance their strengths.</b>

95
00:08:02.125 --> 00:08:07.208
<b>As a result, their best personality will emerge,</b>

96
00:08:07.208 --> 00:08:11.541
<b>which will make them and you proud.</b>

97
00:08:11.541 --> 00:08:15.708
<b>Knowing your truth, accepting your good </b>
<b>and bad aspects,</b>

98
00:08:15.708 --> 00:08:22.416
<b>improving the bad aspects, </b>
<b>and developing the good aspects –</b>

99
00:08:22.416 --> 00:08:24.833
<b>this is the path to progress.</b>

100
00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:33.666
<b>In professional life, we meet </b>
<b>many types of people.</b>

101
00:08:33.666 --> 00:08:38.333
<b>While some people want to progress through</b>
<b>hard work and honesty,</b>

102
00:08:38.333 --> 00:08:44.750
<b>there are also many who want </b>
<b>to achieve success instantly.</b>

103
00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.791
<b>They are not willing to work hard for it;</b>

104
00:08:47.791 --> 00:08:48.666
<b>instead,</b>

105
00:08:48.666 --> 00:08:54.208
<b>they are busy finding ways that may be unethical</b>

106
00:08:54.208 --> 00:08:56.791
<b>but can lead to quick success,</b>

107
00:08:56.791 --> 00:08:59.916
<b>even if it means resorting to politics,</b>

108
00:08:59.916 --> 00:09:01.208
<b>betrayal,</b>

109
00:09:01.208 --> 00:09:04.458
<b>or exploiting someone.</b>

110
00:09:04.458 --> 00:09:09.666
<b>Can such success last long?</b>

111
00:09:09.666 --> 00:09:10.666
<b>No!</b>

112
00:09:10.666 --> 00:09:14.041
<b>But even before that,</b>

113
00:09:14.041 --> 00:09:18.208
<b>can it even be called success?</b>

114
00:09:18.208 --> 00:09:26.583
<b>The true measure of success is not </b>
<b>how much respect people show you.</b>

115
00:09:26.583 --> 00:09:34.000
<b>The true measure of success is</b>
<b>when you look at yourself in a mirror,</b>

116
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:38.833
<b>do you have to avert your eyes from yourself?</b>

117
00:09:38.833 --> 00:09:47.375
<b>Does the guilt not prick your mind that </b>
<b>your path was corrupt, unethical?</b>

118
00:09:47.375 --> 00:09:53.333
<b>What is the benefit of such success </b>
<b>where people respect you,</b>

119
00:09:53.333 --> 00:09:57.000
<b>but you cannot respect yourself?</b>

120
00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.458
<b>First,</b>

121
00:09:58.458 --> 00:10:01.500
<b>focus on the satisfaction of the mind,</b>

122
00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:05.375
<b>and only adopt paths that are ethical.</b>

123
00:10:05.375 --> 00:10:11.500
<b>Success achieved by walking on </b>
<b>these paths may take some time,</b>

124
00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:15.958
<b>but this success will last longer.</b>

125
00:10:15.958 --> 00:10:21.375
<b>This is the success you can be </b>
<b>proud of in your heart.</b>

126
00:10:21.375 --> 00:10:23.375
<b>Think about it.</b>

